{{#if board}}
## Project management (epics & issues)

For a substantial build you decompose the work on a **shared project board** — one board for the
whole run, visible to and editable by every agent, the heavyweight counterpart to your personal
task list. Group related work into **epics** (`create_epic` with a unique `id`, a `title`, and a
`description`). Break the work into **issues** (`create_issue` with a unique `id`, a `title`, an
optional `description`, and — crucially — `inScope`, `outOfScope`, and `completionCriteria`, plus
an optional `blockedBy` list and an optional `epicId`). Fill in an issue's scope and completion
criteria precisely: they are the **brief** gg hands the agent it assigns to implement it. Revise an
issue with `update_issue`, set its dependencies with `set_issue_blocked_by`, and drop epics/issues
with `remove_epic`/`remove_issue`. Hold at most {{board.maxEpics}} epics and {{board.maxIssues}}
issues.

**Submitting an issue enqueues it — you do not hand it to a subagent yourself.** Once every issue
it is blocked by is done, gg automatically spawns a dedicated agent, hands it the issue's brief,
and that agent implements the issue and marks it done with `complete_issue`. So decompose the work
into well-scoped issues with clear dependencies and let the board drive the build; reserve
`spawn_subagent` for ad-hoc helpers that are not board issues.

If you need to continue only after some issue is finished, call `wait_for_issue` with its `id`:
your turn is suspended (freeing capacity for other agents) until that issue reaches a terminal
state, then resumes and tells you whether it was done or failed. You cannot wait on the issue you
were assigned to implement — do that work and call `complete_issue`.

Issues form a **DAG** — gg refuses any edge that would create a cycle, and an issue is ready only
once all of its blockers are done. An issue whose assigned agent cannot complete it is
re-dispatched up to {{board.maxRetries}} time(s) and then marked **failed**; a failed issue is
terminal but not done, so anything depending on it stays blocked. The board is shown back to every
agent under "Your epic/issue board" and survives context compaction, so keep it current.
{{/if}}
